        "id": 1087303
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-31T23:01:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there is one point that we did not have an agreement, that is how coupled/decoupled we want gfxstream to be. But that would be a topic too big for this commit. So let\u0027s modify the name here, and have a separate doc to discuss it.",
      "parentUuid": "d013d932_be0b3a25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "42361f79b2811f82e59a51aa93ed34c0f62e6de0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b91219b_813e0aed",
        "filename": "guest/OpenglSystemCommon/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101621
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-03T15:47:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if we:\n\n1) Land this change with `mesa_log(..)`\n2) Over the next few weeks come up with a strategy on gfxstream-vk/Mesa coupling/upstream/how everything will look like.  I can file a bug on myself and write a doc\n3) Depending on the outcome of larger issue (2), AAOS can definitely commit to changing `mesa_log(..)` to `gfxstream_guest_log(..)`.  It should be mostly a naming change.\n\nDoes that sound like an acceptable plan to you?",
      "parentUuid": "24fe8653_65c38d7e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "42361f79b2811f82e59a51aa93ed34c0f62e6de0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4070e8d8_18c608a4",
        "filename": "guest/OpenglSystemCommon/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087303
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-03T21:40:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would suggest to do it the other way. Once you start using `mesa_log` people will follow and add more mesa dependencies. Then it becomes difficult to clean up.\n\nYou could add a\n```\n#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_ANDROID_KHR\n#define gfxstream_guest_log ALOG\n#else\n#define gfxstream_guest_log mesa_log\n#endif\n```\ninto a header (for example gfxstream_vk_private.h or vk_util.h), then you can reduce the reference to mesa in Android build and can skip dependencies on libmesa_util_c11_gfxstream. If I am reading it correctly, libmesa_util_c11_gfxstream seems to bring in quite some header files (including directX headers), which shouldn\u0027t be part of Android build.\n\nOr we can talk about it in tomorrow\u0027s meeting.",
      "parentUuid": "8b91219b_813e0aed",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "42361f79b2811f82e59a51aa93ed34c0f62e6de0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42c83bf9_1afbf948",
        "filename": "guest/OpenglSystemCommon/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101621
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-04T16:17:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Once you start using mesa_log people will follow and add more mesa dependencies. \n\nI wrote the design doc here:\n\ngoto.google.com/gfxstream-vk-landing-mesa\n\nMy preference is for landing this, since the current design does use Mesa dependencies and doesn\u0027t consider it much of a problem (if up-streamed of-course, which is a Q3 goal).  Curious about other designs :-)  \n\n\u003e reduce the reference to mesa in Android build and can skip dependencies on libmesa_util_c11_gfxstream\n\n`libmesa_util_gfxstream` + `libmesa_util_c11_gfxstream` are currently built when building `libvulkan_enc.a` + `vulkan.ranchu` (the main Vulkan libs).  \n\nSo you won\u0027t save anything at compile-time due to this.  Maybe you can minimize *link-time*, but I wouldn\u0027t worry about that level of optimization too much  just yet.  AOSP has many unnecessary compile-time deps and most people generally don\u0027t care.  For example, the `CommandBufferStagingTests` target in this CL isn\u0027t even used and we can probably delete it :-)\n\nWe have landed build-time optimizations with Mesa in the past:\n\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/26574\n\nWe can always build-time/link-time optimize later after we\u0027re upstream.\n\n\u003e If I am reading it correctly, libmesa_util_c11_gfxstream seems to bring in quite some header files (including directX headers\n\nThere is no DirectX code/headers built.  It\u0027s in the `mesa/include` src, but it\u0027s not built.",
      "parentUuid": "4070e8d8_18c608a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "42361f79b2811f82e59a51aa93ed34c0f62e6de0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
